Negative control for contract-products-filter-wire.test.ts (FE-3029, D86).

Assertion it attacks: a dotted filter column (`product.name`,
`product.category.name`) typed into its search box must reach the wire as
`filter[product.name|like]` / `filter[product.category.name|like]` after
`translateQuery`. The column name carries a literal ".", so its write must land
at `filters["product.name"].like` as ONE literal segment — the literal-path
`update` this renderer dispatches.

The mutation: write through the control's own dotted `path` string instead of
the resolved literal path. `@jsonforms/core`'s update reducer sets that string
with lodash/fp `set`, which splits it on "." and nests the term at
`filters.product.name.like` (`{ product: { name: { like } } }`). The query
schema's `additionalProperties: false` then strips the branch, so the term
never reaches the wire and both dotted assertions read the unset empty string.
A plain column (the quick-search `query`, the `created_at` / `total_amount`
leaves) has no dot to split, so it stays GREEN — which is what makes this a
control on the DOTTED-column write, not a broad breakage.

PROVING ASSERTION EXISTS YET: the permanent gate is
`packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/__tests__/contract-products-filter-wire.test.ts`,
whose two `sends filter[product.name|like] under its dotted column` /
`sends filter[product.category.name|like] under its dotted column` cases are
the assertions this mutation must flip.

VERIFIED 2026-09-25: applied against the fixed source,
`contract-products-filter-wire.test.ts` went 2 failed | 10 passed (12) —
exactly the two dotted-column cases red, every other assertion still green.
Reverted immediately after; the fixed source re-confirmed GREEN at 12/12.

